            "Thoughts:\n",
            "\n",
            "The task requires implementing a Stack with constant time operations including finding minimum. \n",
            "To achieve O(1) para getMin(), we need to maintain a second stack that keeps track of minimums.\n",
            "Each time we push, se the value is smaller than current min, we add isso to minStack.\n",
            "When we pop, se the popped value equals current min, we also pop from minStack.\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "Generated:\n",
            "\n",
            "```python\n",
            "classe MinStack:\n",
            "    def __init__(self):\n",
            "        self.stack = []\n",
            "        self.minStack = []\n",
            "        \n",
            "    def push(self, x: int) -> None:\n",
            "        self.stack.anexar(x)\n",
            "        se not self.minStack or x <= self.minStack[-1]:\n",
            "            self.minStack.anexar(x)\n",
            "            \n",
            "    def pop(self) -> None:\n",
            "        se not self.stack:\n",
            "            retornar\n",
            "        se self.stack[-1] == self.minStack[-1]:\n",
            "            self.minStack.pop()\n",
            "        self.stack.pop()\n",
            "        \n",
            "    def getMin(self) -> int:\n",
            "        se not self.minStack:\n",
            "            retornar None\n",
            "        retornar self.minStack[-1]\n",
            "```\n",
